We will build a simple **"User Manager"** app.
1.  **Backend:** REST API to fetch, add, and manage users (with dummy data).
2.  **Frontend:** React interface to interact with the API.
3.  **Deployment:** How to package and deploy the built code.

---

### Part 1: Project Structure Setup

First, create a folder for your project and separate the backend and frontend.

```bash
mkdir my-fullstack-app
cd my-fullstack-app
```

### Part 2: The Backend (Node/Express)

1.  **Initialize the backend:**
    ```bash
    mkdir backend
    cd backend
    npm init -y
    npm install express cors nodemon
    ```

2.  **Create `server.js`:**
    This file will act as our API server. It handles requests to add data and fetch it.

    ```javascript
    // backend/server.js
    const express = require('express');
    const cors = require('cors');

    const app = express();
    const PORT = 5000;

    // Middleware
    app.use(cors()); // Allow frontend to talk to backend
    app.use(express.json());

    // --- DUMMY DATA ---
    let users = [
        { id: 1, name: "Alice Johnson", email: "alice@example.com" },
        { id: 2, name: "Bob Smith", email: "bob@example.com" }
    ];

    // --- ROUTES ---

    // 1. GET all users
    app.get('/api/users', (req, res) => {
        res.json(users);
    });

    // 2. POST add a new user
    app.post('/api/users', (req, res) => {
        const { name, email } = req.body;

        if (!name || !email) {
            return res.status(400).json({ message: "Name and email are required" });
        }

        const newUser = {
            id: users.length + 1, // Simple ID generation
            name: name,
            email: email
        };

        users.push(newUser);
        res.status(201).json(newUser);
    });

    // 3. DELETE a user
    app.delete('/api/users/:id', (req, res) => {
        const id = parseInt(req.params.id);
        users = users.filter(user => user.id !== id);
        res.json({ message: `User with ID ${id} deleted` });
    });

    // Start Server
    app.listen(PORT, () => {
        console.log(`Server running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
    });
    ```

3.  **Run Backend:**
    ```bash
    cd backend
    node server.js
    ```
    *(Leave this terminal open)*

